    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as our premier offensive anchor. With a score of 81.88, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a potent combination of a hitter-friendly park, a favorable matchup against a starter with a 4.82 xERA, and a 29-plate-appearance BvP edge that boosts his potential for run production. While **Josh Lowe** (70.29) and **Jacob Wilson** (71.63) also register strong marks, they are buoyed significantly by high-upside ballpark factors and softer pitching matchups, making them our secondary engines for chasing production in the counting categories. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Gunnar Henderson** both carry a 30% rain risk warning, but their high efficiency scores demand inclusion; their ability to capitalize on favorable platoon dynamics outweighs the potential for a weather-shortened outing.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench today involves **Coby Mayo**, who landed just outside our optimal starting nine with a score of 60.58. While **Coby Mayo** benefits from the same park factors that push our starters higher, his projected efficiency fell slightly below the threshold required to displace the current middle infield and utility group. Specifically, the defensive utility and consistent lineup placement of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and the high-ceiling speed profile of our outfield starters created a crowded field that edged out his production forecast. We are also closely monitoring the lineup postings for **Drake Baldwin**, **Jacob Wilson**, and **Josh Jung**; while their assumed positions in the batting order are baked into their strong scores, any shift down the order could necessitate a re-evaluation of their daily efficiency ratings.",
